        "evidence": "I tried spike s4 at corner 0,0|1,-1|1,0 together with drawer s5 on cell 0,0, and the configurator refused it with SPIKE_CLASH: 'a spike stands at a corner of this cell the drawer (south half) would fill.' With the drawer placed first, it offered no spike socket at that corner either. Drawers are only offered on N/S half bases (a half-e base got no drawer offer), and every drawer fills the half that touches the corners where its cut face ends. So the rule blocks a shared corner whichever part goes first."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "The build has one drawer and one spike on the same cell (0,0), but not at the same corner. The configurator doesn't allow that pairing: a drawer can't share a corner with a spike, whichever goes on first. As the closest version it would accept, the spike stands at a neighbouring corner of the cell that the drawer doesn't fill. check_build shows no rule errors and the parts don't collide. It does warn that the three pieces aren't locked together yet: they could slide apart until joint bolts are added. Cell 1,0 is left over from the attempt at the shared corner and can be removed."
